 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nPRQL parser returns None for queries without FROM clause\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing PRQL queries that don't start with a `from` clause, the parser incorrectly returns `None` instead of processing the query. This affects queries that should be valid PRQL but don't have an explicit FROM clause.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should work but returns None\nresult = sqlglot.parse(\"derive a + 1\", dialect=\"prql\")\nprint(result)  # Expected: parsed query, Actual: None\n\n# This works fine\nresult = sqlglot.parse(\"from x derive a + 1\", dialect=\"prql\") \nprint(result)  # Works as expected\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when trying to parse PRQL queries that don't begin with a `from` statement. The parser should handle these cases gracefully rather than returning `None`.\n</issue>\n",
